# --- never ship secrets -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- huge, and the app degrades gracefully without them ------------------
# semantic/ is 2.3GB of precomputed embeddings; bind.py falls back to
# lexical retrieval via SemanticUnavailable when it is absent.
CQL_converter/semantic/
# engine/ is the JVM+Node CQL toolchain (89MB of node_modules and classes).
# Excluded for SIZE, not because it is unused -- guidelines._lower_and_compile
# puts every lowered rule through cql-to-elm whenever the toolchain is present,
# and test_toolchain.py executes a compiled library against FHIR bundles. What
# a container without it loses is the compile gate: toolchain.available() is
# False, so CQL is written but not compiled, and the run records
# `compiler_available: false` rather than counting an uncompiled rule as a pass.
# Ship engine/ (and drop this line) if the hosted build must compile too.
patient_checker/engine/
# loinc.db is a leftover staging artifact -- nothing in the codebase reads it.
CQL_converter/loinc.db
CQL_converter/demo.db

# --- runtime data, not source -------------------------------------------
# The guideline store is whatever this machine happened to upload; .gitignore
# already excludes it for the same reason. Copying it into the image ships a
# developer's scratch uploads as pre-loaded library entries on the deployed
# site -- an entry with no `owner` is visible to every visitor (_visible_to).
# api.py calls seed_demo_guidelines() on import, which rebuilds the two /demo
# guidelines from the committed bundle.PMC*.json, so a container that starts
# with no store is the intended state, not a degraded one.
patient_checker/guidelines/

# --- source releases: build-time input only, already baked into terms.db --
Loinc_2.83/
RxNorm_full_08032026/
SnomedCT_InternationalRF2_PRODUCTION_20260801T120000Z/

# --- repo cruft ----------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
paper/
Formatting_Instructions_For_NeurIPS_2026/
*.md
!requirements.txt
